  "description": "GETSAB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H152 Ce6 Fe4 N4 O44. From the CIF bond table, Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce10 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Ce11 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce12 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe8 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 48 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.195-3.937 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.23-127.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe4Ce6O8(ap)4((CH3)3CCO2)12(CH3CO2)4] (analyzed as 1·4H2O; crystallographic C80H144Ce6Fe4N4O44).",
